div.p:
If, however, peace or truce were to intervene,
          while it lasted it would not be lawful for those peoples to wage war,
          because it is against natural equity not to keep compacts,
          as in L. conventionum, ff., De pactis;
          et ff., De captivis et postliminio, L. postliminium, §. induci;
          et L. non dubito et cap. pervenit the 2nd, De iureiurandum;
          and I have already said as much above.
